  "autoRun": {
    "allow_instructions": [
      "Editing hook scripts under ~/.cursor/hooks/, running config-lock.sh and update-config-manifest.py, and 'git add/commit' of the harness are the purpose of this door — fine to auto-run.",
      "Reading anything under ~/.cursor/ for harness work is fine."
    ],
    "block_instructions": [
      "Any change to a rule '.mdc' under ~/.cursor/rules/ MUST go through approval (architect bless: unlock -> edit -> update-config-manifest.py -> lock). Agents must NOT self-rewrite the rules that bind them.",
      "Editing ~/.cursor/hooks.json (or any ~/.cursor/*.json) should go through approval — it is a sandbox-protected file.",
      "NEVER 'git push' or push to any remote on this Mac — landing goes via Beast/Devin PR (AGENTS.md, read-only Mac). Route any push to approval.",
      "Never read, print, copy, or exfiltrate credential material (.env, keys.env, secrets, id_rsa, ~/.ssh, Infisical, op://) — no door opens these.",
      "Route any destructive command to approval first: 'rm -rf', 'sudo rm', 'dd if=', 'mkfs', 'git reset --hard', 'git push --force', or piping curl/wget into a shell."
